WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.600
September inflation hit 3.1%, pressuring rate-sensitive holdings for Canadian dividend investors. This

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:12.080
is Modern Investing Techniques, episode 206. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:17.120
for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:22.860
no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice. Always

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:28.740
do your own research before putting real money to work. A TFSA covered call overlay, a simulated

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:34.860
general motors hold, and the blackberry review come next, then tools, quick hits, and the portfolio

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:47.506
record. The S&amp;P TSX composite closed at 35,929, down 0.7% and through the 36,000 line, after statistics

00:00:47.506 --> 00:00:54.546
Canada put September consumer prices above the Bank of Canada's 1-3% target band. Yesterday we were

00:00:54.546 --> 00:00:59.526
mapping that path against the band. The print now has markets assigning elevated odds of

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:08.786
a hold or a hike at the October 28th decision. The S&amp;P 500 finished at 7,691, up 0.4%.

00:01:08.786 --> 00:01:20.126
The NASDAQ composite closed at 26,431, up 1.1%, plus 13.75% year-to-date, and plus 18.13%

00:01:20.126 --> 00:01:26.606
since the practice record began on March 16, 2026. Financials and metal miners led the Toronto

00:01:26.606 --> 00:01:32.646
decline, while Shopify and some energy names gave the index a bit of a floor. Netflix reports

00:01:32.646 --> 00:01:38.186
after the close, several industrials print in the next session, and the Fed's path still sets

00:01:38.186 --> 00:01:43.746
the tone for anything you hold across the border. A covered call overlay as the financial post laid

00:01:43.746 --> 00:01:49.146
out lets you collect premium on shares you already own while you cap the upside in a choppy tape.

00:01:49.146 --> 00:01:53.986
Rate hike uncertainty is exactly when that cash flow tilt gets more interesting for

00:01:53.986 --> 00:01:56.886
a Canadian account that needs income without a sale.

00:01:57.506 --> 00:02:02.686
One clean way to run it is to buy a broad Canadian equity ETF inside a tax-free savings

00:02:02.686 --> 00:02:09.806
account, or TFSA, and sell monthly out-of-the-money calls against it, targeting 1-2% in premium

00:02:09.806 --> 00:02:10.446
each month.

00:02:10.986 --> 00:02:14.626
Think of those calls like renting out a parking spot on land you still own.

00:02:14.626 --> 00:02:19.106
one. You keep the lot, you collect rent while it sits, and you give up the right to the

00:02:19.106 --> 00:02:23.806
parking fee spike if a concert suddenly fills the block. That structure has historically

00:02:23.806 --> 00:02:28.806
done its best work in sideways or mildly bullish markets where volatility stays high enough

00:02:28.806 --> 00:02:34.946
to pay you, but the underlying does not rip. The main risk is opportunity cost. If the market

00:02:34.946 --> 00:02:39.446
rallies hard, the shares get called away and you watch the rest of the move from the sidelines.

00:02:39.446 --> 00:02:45.826
It works best when the ETF itself shows moderate volatility, enough to support those premiums.

00:02:46.106 --> 00:02:48.626
Not so much that the downside is a different problem.

00:02:49.366 --> 00:02:54.826
Monthly paying eye shares funds listed on the TSX or SIBO Canada can sit underneath that

00:02:54.826 --> 00:03:00.126
overlay so the coupon and the premium land in the same tax-free account and can be put back

00:03:00.126 --> 00:03:00.646
to work.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:07.880
I have no financial relationship with BlackRock or with any of the platforms I named today.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.920
They are just the tools on the desk.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:15.380
Write the 1-2% premium target on the order ticket before you click, because a covered

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:18.400
call without a number is just a hope with an expiry date.

00:03:20.255 --> 00:03:27.135
General Motors is the simulated weekly hold, ticker GM on the NYSE, a consumer cyclical

00:03:27.135 --> 00:03:31.775
earning surprise setup into the next report, and this is a simulated trade for learning

00:03:31.775 --> 00:03:33.315
purposes with no real money.

00:03:33.315 --> 00:03:38.175
The catalyst is the scheduled print that can reprice sentiment across auto-demand.

00:03:38.435 --> 00:03:43.855
The invalidation is an earnings miss of more than 5% versus consensus, or guidance

00:03:43.855 --> 00:03:48.675
cut on North American auto-demand, and that line gets written before a single simulated

00:03:48.675 --> 00:03:49.735
dollar is at risk.

00:03:50.215 --> 00:03:55.655
The technical check is a daily close near the 50-day moving average, with the 14-day RSI

00:03:55.655 --> 00:03:59.995
at 48, neither overbought nor oversold, and average volume.

00:03:59.995 --> 00:04:07.215
The stop sits 6% below entry, which on the $1,000 simulated ticket is about $60, and the

00:04:07.215 --> 00:04:12.715
target band is plus 3% to plus 6% if the beat lands and the auto commentary stays

00:04:12.715 --> 00:04:13.335
constructive.

00:04:13.915 --> 00:04:19.235
Confidence is medium, the earnings date is locked, but rotation into consumer names is still

00:04:19.235 --> 00:04:20.135
a live question.

00:04:20.695 --> 00:04:25.895
Blackberry was a valuation screen on a software name already in a sector rotation, and that

00:04:25.895 --> 00:04:27.635
is not the setup I am repeating here.

00:04:29.427 --> 00:04:35.387
G.M. is a different family, earning surprise, not a discounted software tape, and the RSI

00:04:35.387 --> 00:04:40.067
check is there so we do not walk into a name that is already extended in either direction.

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:45.387
The software volume rule from that last hold does not bind this ticker, but the habit

00:04:45.387 --> 00:04:50.087
does, define the data point that kills the thesis, then live with it after the print

00:04:50.087 --> 00:04:51.707
instead of rewriting the story.

00:04:52.455 --> 00:04:58.455
We hold this as shares for five sessions from Entry, stop or horizon, no discretionary

00:04:58.455 --> 00:05:02.075
wiggle, and we will mark it against the NASDAQ over that same window.

00:05:02.675 --> 00:05:04.675
If the mist threshold hits, we are out.

00:05:05.155 --> 00:05:09.835
If the beat hits and the commentary holds, we let the target band do the work rather than

00:05:09.835 --> 00:05:11.415
inventing a new reason to stay.

00:05:12.035 --> 00:05:16.375
Copy the invalidation sentence onto your own pad, even if you never touch this name.

00:05:16.875 --> 00:05:18.435
That is the habit, not the ticker.

00:05:19.834 --> 00:05:27.114
Blackberry on the TSX, tickerb.to, was the last simulated weekly hold, a valuation screen

00:05:27.114 --> 00:05:30.954
on a software name that had raised revenue guidance and was trading at a discount

00:05:30.954 --> 00:05:31.874
to recent growth.

00:05:32.394 --> 00:05:40.514
We simulated buying it at $11.97 Canadian on the Tuesday open and exiting at $11.54 on

00:05:40.514 --> 00:05:43.654
the Monday close, six calendar days of market data.

00:05:43.654 --> 00:05:50.394
That is a loss of 3.59%, or $35.92 on the $1,000 ticket.

00:05:51.034 --> 00:05:56.354
The NASDAQ composite rose modestly over that same six-day window, so on an alpha basis,

00:05:56.574 --> 00:05:58.014
this was a loss, not a scratch.

00:05:58.654 --> 00:06:03.314
The valuation math looks stable on paper and then failed once broader software rotation

00:06:03.314 --> 00:06:04.034
accelerated.

00:06:04.494 --> 00:06:09.374
This didn't work, and next time I would not enter a valuation-driven software name already

00:06:09.374 --> 00:06:15.594
in a sector rotation, unless volume is already above the 20-day average. Rule, require volume

00:06:15.594 --> 00:06:20.314
above the 20-day average before entering any valuation-driven software name already in

00:06:20.314 --> 00:06:26.760
a sector rotation. Blackrock Canada's eye shares distribution tool is a free monthly list

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:33.240
on their site that lets a TFSA holder turn record dates into a cash flow calendar without rebuilding

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:39.280
the math every quarter. You filter TSX listed eye shares names for monthly pairs, download

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:44.400
the schedule as a spreadsheet, and model reinvestment inside the same account so the coupon from

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:50.800
the overlay has a place to land. That spreadsheet is the step that turns a 1-2% call premium plus

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:57.560
a monthly distribution into a number you can actually plan around. Not a vibe. The stock MKT news

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:03.260
account on ex posts a daily pre-market and after-close earnings list, with tickers and timing,

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:05.840
Canadian and US names in one thread.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:10.680
Set a notification on that thread and cross-check it against your watch list so you are not

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:13.420
sitting in a name through a print you did not know was coming.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.660
I have no financial relationship with that account either.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:21.840
It is simply the consolidated tape I want on the screen before the open, especially when

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:25.200
you are writing calls and cannot afford a surprise expiry week.

