00:08:44.569 --> 00:08:50.809
The rules based simulated book, restarted on August 18, 2026, uses fixed five session

00:08:50.809 --> 00:08:56.069
holds, entry at the next open, and stop or horizon exits with no discretionary calls.

00:08:56.529 --> 00:09:00.729
So you can take the pick, the date, and the stop, and rebuild every number we read.

00:09:01.249 --> 00:09:07.509
Matched window alpha versus the NASDAQ is minus 34.8% across 32 rules based trades.

00:09:07.509 --> 00:09:13.829
The older published history is 83 simulated tickets, a 52% win rate, and a cumulative

00:09:13.829 --> 00:09:22.569
P&amp;L of minus $42.68, with an average of minus 0.05% per trade. Best trade in that history

00:09:22.569 --> 00:09:30.069
is plus 20.11%, worst is minus 27.14%. And the current streak is 3 wins.

00:09:32.318 --> 00:09:36.648
The method is learning from that software rotation miss and keeping the volume filter

00:09:36.648 --> 00:09:41.808
on valuation names. The 32-trade window is the one that can actually be judged against

00:09:41.808 --> 00:09:47.668
the index. Suppose you bought a TSX energy name at the open on October 19, looking

00:09:47.668 --> 00:09:52.368
for a rebound after the inflation print, and by midday the stock had fallen through its

00:09:52.368 --> 00:09:57.788
50-day moving average and kept going. The 50-day and 200-day moving averages are dynamic

00:09:57.788 --> 00:10:03.308
support and resistance that a lot of algorithms and desks actually watch, so a break can invite

00:10:03.308 --> 00:10:07.448
more selling from systematic flows rather than from a person changing their mind.

00:10:07.988 --> 00:10:12.048
The 50-day line is just the average closing price of the prior 50 sessions.

00:10:12.468 --> 00:10:17.908
The 200-day line is the longer trend, and price above both is treated as an uptrend until a

00:10:17.908 --> 00:10:23.528
sustained break below the 50-day starts to look like momentum loss, especially of volume as rising.

00:10:24.108 --> 00:10:30.588
RSI on the 14-day setting, a 0-100-speed gauge, would have needed a reading below 30 to even

00:10:30.588 --> 00:10:36.148
argue oversold, and even then, a bounce attempt wanted volume above the 20-day average before

00:10:36.148 --> 00:10:41.568
it counted as participation. A working habit is to mark the prior days low as first support

00:10:41.568 --> 00:10:45.528
and put the alert there instead of guessing which way the next candle wants to go.

00:10:46.148 --> 00:10:51.888
MACD can flash when its two exponential averages cross, and patterns like double bottoms or flags

00:10:51.888 --> 00:10:57.568
can look like timing edges at known support, but those signals fail more often than not unless volume

00:10:57.568 --> 00:11:00.908
confirms and you have a hard invalidation under the pattern low.

00:11:01.468 --> 00:11:05.508
The misconception is treating a moving average cross as a guaranteed reversal.

00:11:06.048 --> 00:11:11.648
The fix is to demand volume confirmation and a second indicator such as RSI before you

00:11:11.648 --> 00:11:12.428
act on the cross.

00:11:13.088 --> 00:11:15.408
These tools time entries and exits together.

00:11:15.948 --> 00:11:19.688
They do not predict direction which still belongs to the fundamental work.

00:11:22.329 --> 00:11:23.809
Open your platform this week.

00:11:23.809 --> 00:11:27.329
Pull the 50-day moving average on one TSX holding.

00:11:27.829 --> 00:11:32.709
Set a price alert 2% below that line and write the current RSI next to it so both

00:11:32.709 --> 00:11:35.049
numbers are sitting there if the level gets tested.

